A(3,'Your cable-and-sign reference',E('Joint: ΣFₓ = 0 and ΣFᵧ = 0<br>Beam: use Στ = 0 first, then force balance')+P('Identify the angle reference, resolve tension, separate full tension from its components, and state the hinge resultant if requested.'));
s.mc('An angled cable’s vertical component, angle above horizontal, is…',['T cosθ','T sinθ','T itself'],1,'The vertical side is opposite the angle.');s.mc('Unequal cable angles generally give…',['equal tensions','unequal tensions','zero net weight'],1,'Their horizontal components must cancel while vertical components support the weight.');s.mc('For a horizontal beam, the cable horizontal component has torque about its hinge…',['zero if its line passes through the hinge','TL','always maximum'],0,'The perpendicular lever arm is zero.');s.mc('A cable strength rating should be compared with…',['only Tᵧ','full tension T','beam weight alone'],1,'The cable carries the full tensile force.');s.mc('A symmetric support with nearly horizontal cables needs…',['small tensions','large tensions','zero tensions'],1,'T = W/(2sinθ) grows as θ becomes small.');s.mc('A pin hinge can supply…',['a reaction force with two components','a reaction moment in the ideal frictionless model','only an upward force'],0,'An ideal pin balances force but does not resist rotation with a moment.');s.finish();
